    "modeledDistancesCm": "400 m, 800 m, 1500 m, 1 mile and 1-42 km other than 5 km, 10 km, half-marathon and marathon",
    "estimatedPercentileTargets": {},
    "beginnerRule": "Accessible extension beyond fastest 90%, preserving prior beginner ceiling where more generous; not a measured percentile",
    "method": "For 400 m through 4 km, only the world_elite SUB limit is recalibrated against a demanding men's international-level benchmark inspired by the 2025 World Athletics scoring tables; non-standard 1 km, 2 km and 4 km values are modeled from adjacent event standards. The other six tiers retain their previous finisher-percentile-derived thresholds except the 1 km, whose seven levels are manually calibrated as second-resolution targets. Second-resolution limits apply to 400 m, 800 m, 1 km, 1500 m and the mile. Minute-resolution limits remain for 2 km, 3 km and 4 km. For other distances, published percentiles and log-log time/distance interpolation remain unchanged.",
    "ultraDistanceException": "43-200 km retains historical Legend independent of pace: mixed ultra routes cannot support verified common worldwide time percentiles",
    "interpretation": "For distances from 400 m through 4 km, world_elite means a demanding international-level performance benchmark inspired by men's World Athletics scoring tables, not a measured percentile and not a world-record claim. The other tiers retain approximate worldwide shares of recorded race finishes, not official rankings. A SUB card is a time interval, not proof of a ratified record."
